  "question": {
    "text": "One $\\mathrm{Kg}$ of copper is drawn into a wire of $1 \\mathrm{~mm}$ diameter and a wire of $2 \\mathrm{~mm}$ diameter. The resistance of the two wires will be in the ratio"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$2: 1$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$1: 2$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$16: 1$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$4: 1$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Mass $=\\left(\\pi \\mathrm{r}_1^2 \\ell_1\\right) \\sigma$ (Ist wire)\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\text { Mass }=\\left(\\pi \\mathrm{r}_1^2 \\ell_2\\right) \\sigma(2 \\text { nd wire) } \\\\ & \\left(\\pi \\mathrm{r}_1^2 \\ell_1\\right) \\sigma=\\left(\\pi \\mathrm{r}_2^2 \\ell_2\\right) \\sigma\\end{aligned}$\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\left(\\pi \\mathrm{r}_1^2 \\ell_1\\right) \\sigma=\\left(\\pi \\mathrm{r}_2^2 \\ell_2\\right) \\sigma \\\\ & \\frac{\\ell_1}{\\ell_2}=\\left(\\frac{r_2}{r_1}\\right)^2\\end{aligned}$\n$\\frac{R_1}{R_2}=\\frac{\\rho \\frac{\\ell_1}{A_1}}{\\rho \\frac{\\ell_2}{A_2}}=\\frac{\\ell_1}{\\ell_2} \\times \\frac{A_2}{A_1}=\\frac{\\ell_1}{\\ell_2} \\times\\left(\\frac{r_2}{r_1}\\right)^2$\n$\\begin{aligned} & =\\left(\\frac{r_2}{r_1}\\right)^4 \\\\ & \\Rightarrow 16: 1\\end{aligned}$"
  }
